  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Features\n\nMembers with a scoped parameter that return a span or take one by ref or out (#281, part of #201). These no longer report IMP009. The same goes for a params span, which is scoped implicitly, and for an indexer with a span value and a scoped or params key. Generated code repeats scoped wherever it declares the parameter again. C# doesn't infer scoped for a lambda that leaves out its parameter types, so a lambda passed to Returns for such a member declares them: .Returns((scoped ReadOnlySpan\\<char> text) => ...).\n\nEvent spans by ref or out, and spans of async events (#285, part of #201). Raise passes a ref or out span by reference. For an async delegate, RaiseAsync takes the array the span covers, and the handlers get a span over it.\n\nStill IMP009 (see Limitations): custom ref structs, type parameters that allow ref structs, a span returned by reference, and a span an async event's delegate takes by ref, out or ref readonly.\n\nFixes\n\nEvents whose delegate takes a ref or out parameter (#284, closes #282). Their imposters compile now. A handler's change to a ref argument reaches the raiser, and an out argument starts as the default.\n\nInternal\n\nThe generator's code was reorganised without changing what it generates:\n\nthe property and indexer accessors' EnsureConfigured, verification and constructor builders are shared (#279, closes #231);\n\nfield-storing constructors are built with one helper (#283, closes #280).",
